---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import ResourcePageLayout from "../../../layouts/ResourcePageLayout.astro";
---

<ResourcePageLayout
  title="mempool.space — Guide"
  description="Understand the elements shown on mempool.space — Bitcoin's blockchain explorer. Learn about blocks, fees, mempool statistics, and much more."
  lang="en"
>
  <section class="nav-buttons">
    <a href="/en/mining/mining-for-heating" class="nav-btn"
      >Mining for heating</a
    >
    <a href="/en/mining/solo-mining" class="nav-btn">Solo Mining</a>
    <a href="/en/learn/bitcoin-blockchain" class="nav-btn"
      >The Bitcoin Blockchain</a
    >
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <p>
      <a href="https://mempool.space" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
        <Image src="/images/logos/mempool.png" alt="mempool.space" width={500} height={125} class="section-logo" />
      </a>
      <strong>
        .space is Bitcoin's most widely used open source blockchain explorer.
        This page explains all the elements you see when you open
        mempool.space.
      </strong>
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href="https://mempool.space" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
        Open mempool.space →
      </a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- BLOCK VISUALIZATION -->
  <section class="content-section">
    <h2>Block visualization</h2>
    <p>
      The horizontal row of blocks at the top of the page is the heart of
      mempool.space. The blocks are divided into two types, each with its own
      color:
    </p>
    <div class="block-legend">
      <div class="block-item block-green">
        <div class="block-preview green"></div>
        <div class="block-info">
          <strong>Green blocks — Upcoming</strong>
          <p>
            Projected blocks that haven't been mined yet. The contents update
            continuously in real time as miners prioritize transactions.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="block-item block-purple">
        <div class="block-preview purple"></div>
        <div class="block-info">
          <strong>Purple blocks — Confirmed</strong>
          <p>
            Blocks that have already been mined and added to the blockchain.
            Shows fee rate (sat/vB), time, and number of transactions.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="hint">
      💡 Each block shows: number of transactions, median fee (sat/vB), size
      (MB), and time.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- FEE ESTIMATES -->
  <section class="content-section">
    <h2>Fee estimates</h2>
    <p>
      Below the block visualization, recommended fee levels are shown in
      <strong>satoshis per virtual byte (sat/vB)</strong>. The higher the fee, the
      faster the confirmation.
    </p>
    <div class="fee-table">
      <div class="fee-row">
        <div class="fee-badge high">
          <Image src="/images/icons/run.png" alt="" width={1024} height={1024} class="fee-icon" />
          High priority
        </div>
        <div class="fee-desc">
          <strong>Next block (~10 min)</strong> — Use for time-critical transactions.
          The most expensive choice.
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="fee-row">
        <div class="fee-badge medium">
          <Image src="/images/icons/star.png" alt="" width={1024} height={1024} class="fee-icon" />
          Medium
        </div>
        <div class="fee-desc">
          <strong>1–3 blocks (~10–30 min)</strong> — Good for most normal transfers.
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="fee-row">
        <div class="fee-badge low">
          <Image src="/images/icons/timeglas.png" alt="" width={1024} height={1024} class="fee-icon" />
          Low priority
        </div>
        <div class="fee-desc">
          <strong>Can take hours or days</strong> — A cheap option if you're not in
          a hurry.
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="fee-row">
        <div class="fee-badge none">
          <Image src="/images/icons/calendar.png" alt="" width={1024} height={1024} class="fee-icon" />
          No rush
        </div>
        <div class="fee-desc">
          <strong>Waits until the network is quiet</strong> — The lowest possible
          fee. Unpredictable waiting time.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="hint">
      ⚠️ The estimates are guidance only — during busy periods the median fee can
      rise quickly. Always check the current block visualization for the precise
      figures.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- MEMPOOL STATISTICS -->
  <section class="content-section">
    <h2>Mempool statistics</h2>
    <p>Key figures about the network's current state:</p>
    <div class="stats-grid">
      <div class="stat-card">
        <div class="stat-title">Unconfirmed transactions</div>
        <p>
          The total number of transactions waiting to be mined. A high number
          means the network is busy and fees are rising.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="stat-card">
        <div class="stat-title">Memory Usage</div>
        <p>
          How much memory the pending transactions take up. Max ~300 MB per node.
          When exceeded, cheap transactions are dropped.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="stat-card">
        <div class="stat-title">Purging</div>
        <p>
          When the mempool is full, transactions with fees that are too low are
          automatically dropped to free up space.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="stat-card">
        <div class="stat-title">Difficulty Adjustment</div>
        <p>
          Forecast for the change in mining difficulty. <strong>+%</strong> = blocks
          are mined faster than 10 min (difficulty rises). <strong>−%</strong> = blocks
          are mined slower (difficulty falls).
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SEARCH FUNCTION -->
  <section class="content-section">
    <h2>The search function</h2>
    <p>At the top of the page you can search for three types of data:</p>
    <div class="search-items">
      <div class="search-item">
        <Image src="/images/icons/search.png" alt="" width={1024} height={1024} class="search-icon-img" />
        <div>
          <strong>Transaction ID (TXID)</strong>
          <p>
            Find a specific transaction and see its status — whether it's waiting
            in the mempool or confirmed.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="search-item">
        <Image src="/images/icons/lookup.png" alt="" width={1024} height={1024} class="search-icon-img" />
        <div>
          <strong>Bitcoin address</strong>
          <p>See the history and balance of any Bitcoin address.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="search-item">
        <img
          src="/images/icons/blockchain.png"
          alt=""
          class="search-icon-img"
        />
        <div>
          <strong>Block hash or block number</strong>
          <p>
            Explore the contents of a specific block and see all the transactions
            in it.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- NETWORKS -->
  <section class="content-section">
    <h2>Networks and navigation</h2>
    <p>
      Via the dropdown menu in the top left (the Bitcoin logo), you can switch
      between four networks:
    </p>
    <div class="network-list">
      <div class="network-item">
        <span class="network-dot" style="background:#f7931a;"></span>
        <div>
          <strong>Mainnet</strong>
          <p>
            The real Bitcoin network. This is where all real transactions with
            real value take place.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="network-item">
        <span class="network-dot" style="background:#a855f7;"></span>
        <div>
          <strong>Signet</strong>
          <p>
            A controlled test network with centrally managed blocks. More stable
            than Testnet — used by developers to test software.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="network-item">
        <span class="network-dot" style="background:#22c55e;"></span>
        <div>
          <strong>Testnet3</strong>
          <p>
            The older public test network. Coins have no real value. Used to try
            out transactions without risk.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="network-item">
        <span class="network-dot" style="background:#22c55e;"></span>
        <div>
          <strong>Testnet4</strong>
          <p>
            The newest generation of Bitcoin's public test network. Gradually
            replacing Testnet3 for developers.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SETTINGS BAR -->
  <section class="content-section">
    <h2>Settings (footer)</h2>
    <p>
      At the top of the footer you'll find a number of dropdown menus to customize
      the display:
    </p>
    <div class="settings-grid">
      <div class="setting-item">
        <span class="setting-label">Language</span>
        <p>Change the language of the whole site. Danish is available.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="setting-item">
        <span class="setting-label">Currency</span>
        <p>
          Choose which fiat currency amounts and fees are shown in — e.g. USD, EUR,
          or DKK.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="setting-item">
        <span class="setting-label">Time zone</span>
        <p>Adjust the time zone so block timestamps match your local time.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="setting-item">
        <span class="setting-label">Unit</span>
        <p>Choose whether amounts are shown in BTC or sats (satoshis).</p>
      </div>
      <div class="setting-item">
        <span class="setting-label">Theme</span>
        <p>
          Change the visual theme. "wiz" is a popular community theme with extra
          details.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="setting-item">
        <span class="setting-label">Log in</span>
        <p>
          Create an account to save settings, use the Accelerator, and get access
          to extra features.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ACCELERATOR -->
  <section class="content-section">
    <h2>Mempool Accelerator</h2>
    <p>
      Have you sent a transaction with too low a fee that's now stuck?
      <strong>Mempool Accelerator</strong> lets you pay a premium to push the
      transaction forward in the queue and get it confirmed faster. Find the
      feature directly on the front page or under the specific transaction.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a
        href="https://mempool.space/accelerator"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
      >
        Open Mempool Accelerator →
      </a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- GLOSSARY -->
  <section class="content-section">
    <h2>Glossary — key terms</h2>
    <div class="glossary">
      <div class="glossary-item">
        <dt>sat/vB</dt>
        <dd>
          Satoshis per virtual byte — the unit for Bitcoin transaction fees. Used
          to indicate how much you pay miners to process your transaction.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div class="glossary-item">
        <dt>TXID</dt>
        <dd>
          Transaction ID — a unique 64-character identifier for any Bitcoin
          transaction.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div class="glossary-item">
        <dt>Confirmation</dt>
        <dd>
          The number of blocks mined on top of the block that contains your
          transaction. More confirmations = greater security.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div class="glossary-item">
        <dt>UTXO</dt>
        <dd>
          Unspent Transaction Output — the "change" system Bitcoin uses. Your
          "balance" is the sum of all your UTXOs.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div class="glossary-item">
        <dt>RBF</dt>
        <dd>
          Replace-By-Fee — the ability to replace a pending transaction with a new
          one with a higher fee to speed up confirmation.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div class="glossary-item">
        <dt>Sats / Satoshis</dt>
        <dd>The smallest unit of Bitcoin. 1 BTC = 100,000,000 satoshis.</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="glossary-item">
        <dt>vByte</dt>
        <dd>
          Virtual byte — a unit for measuring transaction size that accounts for
          the SegWit discount.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div class="glossary-item">
        <dt>SegWit</dt>
        <dd>
          Segregated Witness — a Bitcoin upgrade that separates signature data
          from transaction data. It introduced vBytes as a unit, where signature
          data is weighted lower — which reduces fees for SegWit transactions.
        </dd>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <a href="#" class="back-to-top">↑ Back to top</a>
</ResourcePageLayout>

<style>
  /* ── Navigation buttons ── */
  .nav-buttons {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--space-md, 1rem);
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .nav-btn {
    flex: 1;
    min-width: 150px;
    text-align: center;
    padding: 0.75rem 1.5rem;
    background-color: var(--primary);
    color: #000;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    border-radius: 6px;
    border: 1px solid var(--primary);
    transition: all 0.3s ease;
  }

  .nav-btn:hover {
    background-color: transparent;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  /* ── Section logo ── */
  .section-logo {
    height: 26px;
    object-fit: contain;
    vertical-align: middle;
    margin-right: 0.5rem;
  }

  /* ── Content sections ── */
  .content-section {
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: var(--text-light, #ccc);
  }

  .content-section h2 {
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md, 1rem);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-sm, 0.5rem);
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(247, 147, 26, 0.2);
  }

  .content-section p {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  /* ── Block legend ── */
  .block-legend {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin: 1.25rem 0;
  }

  .block-item {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1rem;
    align-items: flex-start;
    padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
    border-radius: 8px;
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.04);
    border: 1px solid rgba(247, 147, 26, 0.12);
  }

  .block-preview {
    width: 44px;
    height: 56px;
    border-radius: 5px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .block-preview.green {
    background: linear-gradient(160deg, #22c55e, #16a34a);
    box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(34, 197, 94, 0.35);
  }

  .block-preview.purple {
    background: linear-gradient(160deg, #a855f7, #7c3aed);
    box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(124, 58, 237, 0.35);
  }

  .block-info strong {
    display: block;
    color: var(--text-light, #ccc);
    margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .block-info p {
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    margin: 0;
    color: rgba(204, 204, 204, 0.75);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  /* ── Fee table ── */
  .fee-table {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    margin: 1.25rem 0;
  }

  .fee-row {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.04);
    border-radius: 8px;
    border: 1px solid rgba(247, 147, 26, 0.1);
  }

  .fee-badge {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    width: 180px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    padding: 0.5rem 0.75rem;
    border-radius: 5px;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #fff;
  }

  .fee-icon {
    width: 42px;
    height: 42px;
    object-fit: contain;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    opacity: 0.9;
  }

  .fee-badge.high   { background: #dc2626; }
  .fee-badge.medium { background: #d97706; }
  .fee-badge.low    { background: #2563eb; }
  .fee-badge.none   { background: #4b5563; }

  .fee-desc {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--text-light, #ccc);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .fee-desc strong {
    color: #fff;
  }

  /* ── Hint box ── */
  .hint {
    background: rgba(247, 147, 26, 0.08);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--primary);
    border-radius: 0 6px 6px 0;
    padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: rgba(204, 204, 204, 0.9);
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
  }

  /* ── Stats grid ── */
  .stats-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  .stat-card {
    padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.04);
    border: 1px solid rgba(247, 147, 26, 0.15);
    border-radius: 8px;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .stat-title {
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--primary);
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .stat-card p {
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    color: rgba(204, 204, 204, 0.8);
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* ── Search items ── */
  .search-items {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  .search-item {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1rem;
    align-items: flex-start;
    padding: 0.9rem 1.1rem;
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.04);
    border: 1px solid rgba(247, 147, 26, 0.12);
    border-radius: 8px;
  }

  .search-icon-img {
    width: 36px;
    height: 36px;
    object-fit: contain;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    margin-top: 0.1rem;
    opacity: 0.85;
  }

  .search-item strong {
    display: block;
    color: var(--text-light, #ccc);
    margin-bottom: 0.2rem;
  }

  .search-item p {
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    color: rgba(204, 204, 204, 0.75);
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* ── Network list ── */
  .network-list {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  .network-item {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1rem;
    align-items: flex-start;
    padding: 0.85rem 1.1rem;
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.04);
    border: 1px solid rgba(247, 147, 26, 0.12);
    border-radius: 8px;
  }

  .network-dot {
    width: 14px;
    height: 14px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    margin-top: 0.35rem;
    box-shadow: 0 0 6px currentColor;
  }

  .network-item strong {
    display: block;
    color: var(--text-light, #ccc);
    margin-bottom: 0.15rem;
  }

  .network-item p {
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    color: rgba(204, 204, 204, 0.75);
    margin: 0;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  /* ── Settings grid ── */
  .settings-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  .setting-item {
    padding: 0.85rem 1.1rem;
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.04);
    border: 1px solid rgba(247, 147, 26, 0.12);
    border-radius: 8px;
  }

  .setting-label {
    display: inline-block;
    background: rgba(247, 147, 26, 0.15);
    color: var(--primary);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    padding: 0.15rem 0.55rem;
    border-radius: 4px;
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.03em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .setting-item p {
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    color: rgba(204, 204, 204, 0.75);
    margin: 0;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  /* ── Glossary ── */
  .glossary {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0;
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
    border: 1px solid rgba(247, 147, 26, 0.15);
    border-radius: 8px;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .glossary-item {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 140px 1fr;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(247, 147, 26, 0.1);
  }

  .glossary-item:last-child {
    border-bottom: none;
  }

  .glossary-item dt {
    padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    background: rgba(247, 147, 26, 0.06);
    border-right: 1px solid rgba(247, 147, 26, 0.12);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
  }

  .glossary-item dd {
    padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    color: rgba(204, 204, 204, 0.85);
    margin: 0;
    line-height: 1.6;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
  }

  /* ── Responsive ── */
  @media (max-width: 567px) {
    .nav-buttons {
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .settings-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .block-legend,
    .stats-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .fee-row {
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: flex-start;
    }

    .fee-badge {
      width: auto;
    }

    .glossary-item {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .glossary-item dt {
      border-right: none;
      border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(247, 147, 26, 0.1);
    }
  }
</style>
